@PizzaExpressLive_regression @PE-76
Feature: Sitemaps

  PE-76 SPX-05. There is no /sitemap.xml: robots.txt lists six sitemaps under
  /sitemaps/ (confirmed live on staging and production, 2026-11-13). They are
  regenerated by the scheduled sitemap tasks, so a task broken by the upgrade
  shows up here as a missing or empty sitemap.

  Scenario: robots.txt points at the sitemaps
    When I GET the site path "/robots.txt"
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the response body should contain "/sitemaps/products.xml"
    And the response body should contain "/sitemaps/content.xml"

  Scenario Outline: The <sitemap> sitemap is served
    When I GET the site path "/sitemaps/<sitemap>.xml"
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the response body should contain "<urlset"

    Examples:
      | sitemap            |
      | products           |
      | content            |
      | articles           |
      | categories         |
      | article_categories |
      | locations          |

  Scenario: URLs in the content sitemap resolve
    When I GET the site path "/sitemaps/content.xml"
    Then 10 URLs sampled from the sitemap response should each return status 200

